# Base URL

The production API endpoint will be published before the official public release.

Example:

```
https://api.codexeron.com
```

---

# Authentication

Every protected endpoint requires authentication.

Authentication is performed using an API Key.

Never expose your API credentials publicly.

---

# Response Format

All API responses are returned in JSON format.

Example:

```json
{
    "success": true,
    "message": "Request completed successfully.",
    "data": {}
}
```

---

# Versioning

The Codexeron API follows Semantic Versioning.

Example versions:

```
v1
v2
v3
```

Breaking changes are introduced only in major API versions.

---

# Security

The API has been designed with security in mind.

Recommendations:

- Always use HTTPS.
- Protect API Keys.
- Validate responses.
- Handle errors properly.
- Respect rate limits.
- Never expose sensitive credentials.

---

# Best Practices

For reliable integrations:

- Use the latest API version.
- Validate all responses.
- Handle network failures gracefully.
- Implement retry logic where appropriate.
- Monitor API usage.

